{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1558407-chthonians","id":1558407,"title":"Chthonians","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-21T06:04:25-08:00","id":1558407,"title":"Chthonians","content":"I know Mage gives them little more than a paragraph, and they get a lot more detail in the Geist core. But a few questions.<br /> <br /> Do they have any language, culture/community? Do they have larger goals or intentions? Have they become corrupted as the Underworld was? Their nature's affected by the changes which occured (ie the islands and eventually caverns which emerged from the Ocean of Fragments as more and more ghosts fell in and eventually figured out to hang on/be absorbed into the walls, instead of dissolving...).<br /> <br /> Is it possible that these Underworld natives are not fans of what the Underworld has become? Or that eating too many ghosts would corrupt them in some way?<br /> <br /> Any suggestions for plot hooks or other things to make the chthonians more interesting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T06:40:57-08:00","id":1558408,"title":"","content":"Most of the information on Chthonians before Geist can be found in the Mage 1e supplement <i>Summoners</i>, with another brief paragraph in the Geist 1e corebook.<br /> <br /> The short version is that they have always been a big fat Mystery.<br /> <br /> They're made up of upsetting imagery of death (and those forms of life associated with scavenging and mortality), they have Influence over Death that they can use like mages use the Death Arcanum, they're drawn back toward the Underworld if they ever find themselves in the living world, conversation doesn't seem to be a conscious process for them, and trying to read their minds runs the risk of giving you a derangement for at least a couple months. Theories go that they're so inhuman because they're Supernal casualties of the Fall or that they're ghosts or geists so far gone that they've lost all aspects of their humanity, and particularly powerful specimens may have insight into routes from the Underworld into the Lower Depths in addition to potentially being able to recall information known by ghosts they've consumed.<br /> <br /> 1e had them retreating further into the Underworld as the number of ghosts increased, but 2e makes that clear that that translates more directly to &quot;there's more of them at or around the Rivers for travel reasons.&quot; They're functionally similar to spirits in their inhuman perspective and drive to consume (here only loosely related to survival), but they don't tend to communicate or collaborate in the environment of the Great Below. They are mobile manifestations of the uncaring nature of the Underworld, which is probably why some ghosts worship them as avatars of the Chthonic Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T20:25:03-08:00","id":1558428,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that. I didn't know they were in Summoners.<br /> <br /> Are there any notable differences between editions, apart from what you said about them going deeper into the Underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-21T21:10:43-08:00","id":1558431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1558407-chthonians?p=1558428#post1558428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any notable differences between editions, apart from what you said about them going deeper into the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only that Geist 2e likens the ones in the Rivers to marine life; the Rivers serving as the line of demarcation between the Upper Reaches and the Lower Mysteries means they're still most likely to be encountered well beyond the Avernian Gates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-06T02:29:16-07:00","id":1559801,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I finally got to read the sections of Summoners, and in typical 1e fashion &quot;oh mages are convinced these are former inhabitants of Stygia&quot; I despise. <br /> <br /> But nothing about their description seems relevant to that, and overall they seem alien and unintelligible (not really thinking about what they are asked).<br /> <br /> The interesting points about them moving away from ghosts as the numbers of ghosts increases suggests a possible intentional act which could be interpreted to offer some insights. But canonically, they are just dangerous and not politically motivated.<br /> <br /> If I was to rewrite them, it would be clear they are associated with function of the Underworld, in some fashion and opposed or indifferent to the Reapers. They clearly don't enjoy the overwhelming number of ghosts - but that doesn't seem to be a survival thing for them. Maybe they just enjoy having done a good job, and there being no ghosts in an area fills that criteria. Having ghosts isn't scarey or dangerous, but it just means there is work to be done...<br /> <br /> Like, if they consume a ghost and then swim in the rivers, they could potentially have the ghost's memories dissolve into the river and that is one less thing being absorbed into the walls of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> But this doesn't suit the &quot;ancient knowledge that Mages search out&quot; framing which Summoners is aiming for.<br /> <br /> I'm far more interested in pushing them towards a 2e Geist framing where they are part of a (very broken) Underworld ecology - even if that doesn't suit Mage.<br /> <br /> So headcanon:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>my headcanon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Underworld is supposed to help recycle souls, those that lose their Anchors instead of letting them go and passing on. The Ocean of Fragments is the failsafe to allow desperate ghosts to pass on. And the things that naturally live in it (Chthonic entities) are meant to help reluctant ghosts escape - by consuming them and returning to the Ocean.<br /> <br /> This natural system is deeply broken and the desperation to avoid their fate to hang on is the impetus behind the Chthonic God, the twisted powers of the Underworld that empower Reapers to snatch ghosts away from their Anchors and into the Underworld are driven by fear and resentment. They try to avoid passing on and grow. Every ghost absorbed into the walls of the Underworld is another desperate part of them. Every Dominion to fall into the Ocean of Fragments is a lose in their grip. Every Kerberos functions to serve their desire for rules and order, for something resembling real life... The thing they desperately want, but can only mimic in static laws. A pale reflection of reality...<br /> <br /> The Neverborn Chthonians are exhausted, there are always more ghosts and their never-ending task simply grows. They sometimes satisfy their urge to consume, but they think on a different time-scale to humans, every attempt at communication is like a fly crawling in their skin, to them the living are like unripened food. Not ready to consume, in a world of abundance, or rotting food everywhere. Maybe in the past they sought to undo the damage, but now they try to keep the rivers and shores clear or any blockages, so at least some ghosts can make it to their final destinations.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-08T12:48:17-07:00","id":1559839,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, they could be the embodiment of the death of historical times where death was prominent, such as the bubonic plague, Spanish flu or extinction events","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}